  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 148 PM EDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\n- Showers and storms possible this afternoon into Saturday\n\nThe southerly flow will continue through the day with a westward shift \nof the winds as the day continues. There remains small chances for \nshowers and thunderstorms this afternoon and early evening southeast of \nGrand Rapids. While there remains the potential, the late of \ninstability should stifle convection.  \n\n The best area for storms remains east of Kalamazoo. Latest CAMS \ncontinue to show the dwindling potential for convection.\n Any rainfall should aid the potential for shallow ground fog to reform \nSaturday morning. \n\n- Showers and storms possible late Sunday into Monday\n\n  The next chance for convection will be Sunday into Monday. A large \nupper level low situated over Hudson bay will dominate the pattern \nthrough the first half of next week. This low will drag a mid \nlevel and surface boundary through the region early next week. \nThis will coincide with good PWAT anomalies the are present \nthrough the atmosphere. With mean PATS of 1.5 to 2 inches, along \nwith a slow moving surface boundary over the area Sunday through \nMonday, there will be the potential for heavy rain. As such WPC \nhas Michigan in a marginal risk of excessive rain fall Sunday into\nMonday, and slight risk Monday into Tuesday. So will have to keep\nan eye on how the boundaries set up and move, and or don't move. \nThe biggest area of concern for now is south of the I 96 corridor,\nespecially along and south of the I 94 corridor.\n \n\n- Strong to Severe storms possible late Monday\n\nAs the above mentioned boundary moves southward, it should\ninteract with some warm and moist air as it advects along the\nfrontal. Given the potential for moderate deep layer shear along \nthis boundary, daytime highs in the 80s and dewpoints in the 70s\nSPC already has southern Lower Michigan outlooked for the\npotential for severe storms Monday afternoon and evening. \n There remains a fair amount of questions and interactions to take\nplace though it is something that we will continue to watch.",
